{
  "source_note": "Patch notes for Ledgerline ERP 7.2.3-P6, released on 23 October 2026 and effective at Northbridge Cycles on 26 October 2026. The patch modifies Fetch (po_fetch) to derive tax codes by supplier country and adds an error-blocking option 'B' to the PUR.CERT_CHK parameter.",
  "pages": [
    {
      "slug": "rn-7-2-3-p6",
      "type": "release",
      "title": "RN-7.2.3-P6 Ledgerline ERP 7.2.3-P6 Patch Notes",
      "facts": [
        {"fact": "Ledgerline ERP 7.2.3-P6 was released on 23 October 2026 and installed at Northbridge Cycles on 26 October 2026 at 07:00 under change CR-2026-034.", "quote": "Ledgerline ERP 7.2.3-P6 was released on 23 October 2026 and installed at Northbridge Cycles on 26 October 2026 at 07:00 (change CR-2026-034).", "page": 1, "section": "1. Summary", "sheet": null, "row": null},
        {"fact": "In 7.2.3-P6, Fetch (F3, service po_fetch) fills the tax code from the supplier's country: VAT20-UK for GB suppliers and VAT20-RC for suppliers in any other country.", "quote": "Fetch (F3, service po_fetch) now fills the tax code from the supplier's country: VAT20-UK for a supplier in GB, VAT20-RC for a supplier in any other country.", "page": 1, "section": "2. Changes", "sheet": null, "row": null},
        {"fact": "Before patch 7.2.3-P6, Fetch always populated VAT20-UK, triggering ERR-PO-0412 for overseas suppliers.", "quote": "Before this patch Fetch always filled VAT20-UK, which caused ERR-PO-0412 for overseas suppliers. Orders saved before the patch are not changed.", "page": 1, "section": "2. Changes", "sheet": null, "row": null},
        {"fact": "Parameter PUR.CERT_CHK accepts a third value, 'B' (block), which refuses Save on PUR-PO-01 for items with the lithium-cell flag with ERR-SUP-0208 UN38.3 CERTIFICATE MISSING OR EXPIRED if no valid certificate exists on order date.", "quote": "Parameter PUR.CERT_CHK accepts a third value, B (block). With B, Save on PUR-PO-01 of an order for an item with the lithium-cell flag is refused with ERR-SUP-0208", "page": 1, "section": "2. Changes", "sheet": null, "row": null},
        {"fact": "Under PUR.CERT_CHK, setting value 'Y' continues to only warn with W-SUP-0207, while the parameter default remains 'N'.", "quote": "Y still only warns (W-SUP-0207). The default stays N.", "page": 1, "section": "2. Changes", "sheet": null, "row": null},
        {"fact": "The certificate check in 7.2.3-P6 still evaluates only the valid-to date and does not enforce company rules regarding issue dates or margins.", "quote": "The certificate check still looks only at the valid-to date. It does not apply company rules on issue dates or margins.", "page": 1, "section": "2. Changes", "sheet": null, "row": null},
        {"fact": "At Northbridge Cycles, PUR.CERT_CHK remains set to 'N' following CAB CR-2026-031 to review in January 2027, keeping the manual check in SOP-PUR-001 as the active control.", "quote": "At Northbridge, PUR.CERT_CHK stays N: the change board decided on 7 October 2026 (CR-2026-031) to review the certificate check in January 2027. The manual check in SOP-PUR-001 remains the control.", "page": 1, "section": "3. Effect at Northbridge", "sheet": null, "row": null},
        {"fact": "The automated Fetch tax code behaviour is live at Northbridge from 26 October 2026, meaning buyers no longer need to manually change VAT20-UK to VAT20-RC for overseas suppliers.", "quote": "The new Fetch behaviour is live from 26 October 2026: buyers no longer need to change VAT20-UK to VAT20-RC by hand for overseas suppliers, but should still check the tax code before Save.", "page": 1, "section": "3. Effect at Northbridge", "sheet": null, "row": null}
      ]
    },
    {
      "slug": "screen-pur-po-01",
      "type": "screen",
      "title": "PUR-PO-01 Purchase Order Entry",
      "facts": [
        {"fact": "From 26 October 2026 in 7.2.3-P6, Fetch (F3, po_fetch) on PUR-PO-01 automatically defaults the tax code to VAT20-UK for GB suppliers and VAT20-RC for suppliers in all other countries.", "quote": "Fetch (F3, service po_fetch) now fills the tax code from the supplier's country: VAT20-UK for a supplier in GB, VAT20-RC for a supplier in any other country.", "page": 1, "section": "2. Changes", "sheet": null, "row": null},
        {"fact": "If PUR.CERT_CHK is set to 'B', saving PUR-PO-01 for an item with the lithium-cell flag is refused with ERR-SUP-0208 if the supplier lacks a UN38.3 certificate valid on the order date.", "quote": "With B, Save on PUR-PO-01 of an order for an item with the lithium-cell flag is refused with ERR-SUP-0208 UN38.3 CERTIFICATE MISSING OR EXPIRED when the supplier has no UN38.3 certificate valid on the order date.", "page": 1, "section": "2. Changes", "sheet": null, "row": null}
      ]
    },
    {
      "slug": "services-pur-po",
      "type": "service-group",
      "title": "services-pur-po Purchase Order Services",
      "facts": [
        {"fact": "Service po_fetch fills the tax code as VAT20-UK when the supplier country is GB, and as VAT20-RC for any other supplier country as of 7.2.3-P6.", "quote": "Fetch (F3, service po_fetch) now fills the tax code from the supplier's country: VAT20-UK for a supplier in GB, VAT20-RC for a supplier in any other country.", "page": 1, "section": "2. Changes", "sheet": null, "row": null}
      ]
    },
    {
      "slug": "err-po-0412",
      "type": "error",
      "title": "ERR-PO-0412 TAX CODE DOES NOT MATCH SUPPLIER COUNTRY",
      "facts": [
        {"fact": "Prior to patch 7.2.3-P6, Fetch invariably set VAT20-UK on purchase orders, causing ERR-PO-0412 on overseas supplier orders unless changed manually.", "quote": "Before this patch Fetch always filled VAT20-UK, which caused ERR-PO-0412 for overseas suppliers. Orders saved before the patch are not changed.", "page": 1, "section": "2. Changes", "sheet": null, "row": null}
      ]
    },
    {
      "slug": "err-sup-0208",
      "type": "error",
      "title": "ERR-SUP-0208 UN38.3 CERTIFICATE MISSING OR EXPIRED",
      "facts": [
        {"fact": "ERR-SUP-0208 UN38.3 CERTIFICATE MISSING OR EXPIRED is raised on PUR-PO-01 Save when PUR.CERT_CHK is configured to 'B' and an order line contains a lithium-cell item whose supplier has no UN38.3 certificate valid on the order date.", "quote": "With B, Save on PUR-PO-01 of an order for an item with the lithium-cell flag is refused with ERR-SUP-0208 UN38.3 CERTIFICATE MISSING OR EXPIRED when the supplier has no UN38.3 certificate valid on the order date.", "page": 1, "section": "2. Changes", "sheet": null, "row": null}
      ]
    },
    {
      "slug": "topic-un-38-3-certificates",
      "type": "topic",
      "title": "UN 38.3 Certificates",
      "facts": [
        {"fact": "Ledgerline 7.2.3-P6 introduced option 'B' for parameter PUR.CERT_CHK to strictly block purchase orders for lithium-cell items with ERR-SUP-0208 when UN 38.3 certificates are missing or expired.", "quote": "Parameter PUR.CERT_CHK accepts a third value, B (block). With B, Save on PUR-PO-01 of an order for an item with the lithium-cell flag is refused with ERR-SUP-0208 UN38.3 CERTIFICATE MISSING OR EXPIRED", "page": 1, "section": "2. Changes", "sheet": null, "row": null},
        {"fact": "The automated certificate validation in Ledgerline inspects only the valid-to date and does not enforce Northbridge rules concerning issue dates or safety margins.", "quote": "The certificate check still looks only at the valid-to date. It does not apply company rules on issue dates or margins.", "page": 1, "section": "2. Changes", "sheet": null, "row": null},
        {"fact": "Northbridge maintains PUR.CERT_CHK at 'N' following CR-2026-031 pending review in January 2027, relying instead on manual verification under SOP-PUR-001.", "quote": "At Northbridge, PUR.CERT_CHK stays N: the change board decided on 7 October 2026 (CR-2026-031) to review the certificate check in January 2027. The manual check in SOP-PUR-001 remains the control.", "page": 1, "section": "3. Effect at Northbridge", "sheet": null, "row": null}
      ]
    },
    {
      "slug": "topic-tax-codes",
      "type": "topic",
      "title": "Tax codes",
      "facts": [
        {"fact": "From 26 October 2026 under Ledgerline 7.2.3-P6, Fetch assigns tax code VAT20-UK for GB suppliers and VAT20-RC for non-GB overseas suppliers.", "quote": "Fetch (F3, service po_fetch) now fills the tax code from the supplier's country: VAT20-UK for a supplier in GB, VAT20-RC for a supplier in any other country.", "page": 1, "section": "2. Changes", "sheet": null, "row": null}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "conflicts": [
    {
      "kind": "superseded",
      "other": "man-pur-72",
      "detail": "Patch 7.2.3-P6 supersedes earlier user manuals and guides where Fetch (po_fetch) always populated VAT20-UK by default regardless of supplier country."
    }
  ]
}
